+    Prompt 07: _adaptive_levin_subregion_cc() on the ascending form of x_span, its value negated
+    when x_span is reversed, for the two places prompt 07 calls the nested pair directly (a window
+    piece, and a guarded region at depth_max). _adaptive_levin_subregion_cc() itself ignores the
+    orientation of x_span -- _cc_weights() takes |b - a| -- so on a reversed span its value has
+    the wrong sign; that defect of the existing fallback is recorded, not fixed, by prompt 07 (its
+    log), and is kept out of the new paths here. theta_prime_Cheb enters only through min/max of
+    |theta'| and phase_span through its magnitude, so neither depends on the orientation.
+    """
+    a, b = x_span
